  "interpretation": "This run did not reproduce the multi-second take gap: the maximum interval was 0.392429 s, below the 0.4 s freshness threshold. During that shorter 0.392 s interval, 96 RMW waits returned unread_count=0 and the callback thread successfully returned 308 datagrams from fd 70 bound to UDP port 62427; no receive syscall errors were recorded. This establishes kernel-to-process delivery of datagrams to the participant receive thread in this shorter window, not camera_pose topic identity or insertion into its DataReader history. The interval crossed a map_id reset: MapStatus changed from ready to map_reset_acknowledged and the independent reader saw only one pose. The planner goal probe timed out before ready; instrumentation, map reset, and sparse matched input make this run non-comparable to the #353/#354 long-gap runs.",
